{"step_index":147,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:25:55Z","thinking":"**Applying Remaining Suggestions**\n\nI've just finished Task 144. Now I'm moving on to applying the remaining suggestions. I'll be integrating WorkWeek, ServiceImmediately, and Policy RAG, as well as addressing the Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs) in the framework. Section 5 is next up in the queue, after which there's a quick section missing from your list.\n\n\n**Analyzing Section Details**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics of Sections 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 5, 6, and 7, analyzing the proposed changes in detail. I'm focusing on the exact string matches and comparing the \"Old\" and \"New\" versions. I've already identified several key modifications and nuances in each section, and their implications on the overall design and performance.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"BypassSandbox":true,"CommandLine":"/google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"API calls to WorkWeek must pass a composite authentication token that scopes data retrieval strictly to the specific employee querying the system.\" \"API calls to WorkWeek must pass a composite authentication token (Gateway signed JWT assertion via X-Authenticated-User) that scopes data retrieval strictly to the specific employee querying the system.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"validating that the request does not exceed remaining accrued days.\" \"validating that the request does not exceed remaining accrued days. Default submission status is 'Submitted for Manager Approval'.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"No employee-specific dynamic data should be cached in the AI orchestration layer.\" \"No employee-specific dynamic data should be cached in the AI orchestration layer. Implement a 5-second timeout with exponential backoff (max 2 retries) and circuit-breaker degradation messaging.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"Update Ticket Status: Transition the lifecycle state of a ticket (e.g. to 'Resolved' or 'Closed'), including optional resolution notes.\" \"Cancel Ticket: Allow end-users to transition tickets to 'Canceled' only if the ticket is currently in 'New' state. Transitioning status to 'Resolved' or 'Closed' is restricted to fulfiller roles.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"Duplication Mitigation: Scan for potential duplicate tickets submitted in quick succession before creating new entries.\" \"Duplication Mitigation: Scan for potential duplicate tickets submitted within 15 minutes by the same caller. If semantic similarity on short description > 0.85, prompt user to confirm or append a comment.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"within [X] hours/minutes of the document being updated in the source repository.\" \"within <= 1 hour of the document being updated in the source repository via webhook/CDC triggers, supported by an admin manual sync endpoint and a daily 24-hour batch refresh.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"The system must begin generating a response within 10 seconds. The addition of input/output safety scanning must not add more than 300ms of latency per turn.\" \"Conversational Latency SLAs: (1) Policy Q&A RAG: p50 < 1.5s, p95 < 3.0s; (2) Single-system transactions: p50 < 2.0s, p95 < 4.0s; (3) Cross-system orchestration: p50 < 4.0s, p95 < 7.0s with token streaming. Safety scanning overhead must not add more than 300ms per turn.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"provide instructions for manual follow-up or attempt compensating actions to ensure data consistency.\" \"retain prior successful steps, emit an event to the HR Operations Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ), and provide the user with the successful transaction reference ID.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"The system will use functional test credentials for backend integrations. Integrations with enterprise identity management systems (such as Active Directory, Okta, or Single Sign-On / SSO) are excluded from this release.\" \"To satisfy zero-trust RBAC and origin verification without blocking on enterprise Okta/SSO integration, the Chat UI includes a test persona selector that issues signed JWT assertion headers (X-Authenticated-User) to the API Gateway. Backend adapters connect using sandbox service accounts scoped by the verified caller context.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"100% Detection of known prompt injection/jailbreak test cases; < 1% False Positives (blocking legitimate queries).\" \">= 99.5% Detection of known prompt injection/jailbreak test cases; < 1% False Positives (blocking legitimate queries).\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y && /google/bin/releases/gemini-agents-gdocs/gdocs mutate replace 1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4 \"< 10.0 Seconds average response time; Safety scanning overhead < 300ms.\" \"Policy Q&A p95 < 3.0s; Chained workflows p95 < 7.0s; Safety scanning overhead < 300ms.\" --tab t.tpcr3esq94y","Cwd":"/google/src/cloud/gauravrawat/summarize_latest_chats/google3","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Applying tracked changes to Sections 4, 5, 6, 7","toolSummary":"Suggest edits for remaining sections"}}]}
