{"step_index":153,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:26:45Z","content":"A new document has been created with **native Google Docs Tracked Changes (Suggesting Mode)** enabled for all revisions:\n\n🔗 **[HR Agentic Solution BRD - With Tracked Changes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tHkqwbPOJ2HUlmTliaR-Ip0gnpAhxiIrXKcJxu0qlT4/edit)**\n\n---\n\n### What You Can Do in This Document:\n* **Interactive Review & Acceptance:** Every proposed change is displayed as a native Google Docs suggestion (with inline strikethroughs for deleted text, green text for additions, and individual **Accept [✓] / Reject [✗]** cards in the right-hand margin).\n* **Integrated Comment Threads:** All 17 architectural and requirements comment threads with our approved resolutions remain anchored in context alongside the suggestions.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Tracked Changes Available for Review in the Doc:\n\n1. **Executive Summary:** Replaced unauthenticated service account statements with the **Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer** (`X-Authenticated-User` signed JWT) to satisfy zero-trust RBAC in MVP 1.\n2. **Section 1 (Objectives):**\n   * Grounded the **40% deflection metric** against an explicit baseline of **5,000 Tier-1 tickets/month** (target 2,000 deflected inquiries/month by Month 6).\n   * Converted \"zero policy violations\" to probabilistic safety benchmarks ($\\ge 99.5\\%$).\n3. **Section 2 & 2.3 (Scope):** Formally marked **UC-2.3 (Relocation & Facilities Badging)**, payroll processing, and multi-lingual capabilities as **Out of Scope for MVP 1** (deferred to Phase 2).\n4. **Section 3 (Use Cases):**\n   * **UC-1.2:** Standardized leave balances and prompts strictly to **work days**.\n   * **UC-2.1:** Added mandatory **Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) Confirmation Cards** before ordering equipment.\n   * **UC-2.2:** Added **Forward Escalation with Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)** error handling.\n5. **Section 4 (Functional Requirements):**\n   * **FR-1.5 (RBAC):** Added gateway-level identity scoping to prevent prompt-based cross-user data leakage.\n   * **FR-3.2 (WorkWeek):** Added `Submitted for Manager Approval` default state and company holiday/weekend exclusion rules.\n   * **FR-3.4 (WorkWeek):** Configured a 5-second timeout, 2 retries, and circuit-breaker degradation messaging.\n   * **FR-4.2 (ServiceImmediately):** Restricted status changes to 'Canceled' for end-users, reserving 'Resolved'/'Closed' for fulfillers.\n   * **FR-4.3 (ServiceImmediately):** Added concrete 15-minute / cosine similarity $>0.85$ deduplication heuristics.\n   * **FR-5.5 (Policy RAG):** Set knowledge base sync SLA to $\\le 1\\text{ hour}$ with CDC/webhook triggers.\n6. **Section 5 (NFRs):** Defined granular latency SLAs ($p50 < 1.5\\text{s}, p95 < 3.0\\text{s}$ for RAG; $p95 < 7.0\\text{s}$ for chained workflows) and DLQ error recovery.\n7. **Section 6 (Constraints):** Formalized the test persona selector and Gateway JWT architecture."}
